From d830a07c7794ad8ae3005af1f44f66dd46be27f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Grinberg <igrinberg@habana.ai>
Date: Mon, 30 Nov 2020 02:10:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [SW-20141] gaudi: add fw hard reset support

Add FW hard reset sequence flow to fix the rare bug when a transaction
is stuck in the PCIE_IF and prevents the chip from normal execution
after the reset.
As a part of the new reset flow the PCIe is closed for accesses in both,
the memory space access and the ELBI access. Therefore the new reset
sequence depends on the fact that after the reset Ppboot knows to open
the PCIe for requests.

Change-Id: I8e0426ea4b4574357aa3db5803f804c19b4a320f
Signed-off-by: Igor Grinberg <igrinberg@habana.ai>
(cherry picked from commit 9c26766b6f070a5a3abe548d7081a8c9d7ee57b7)
---

diff --git a/common/boot_if.c b/common/boot_if.c
index e0f9e21..6badf23 100644
--- a/common/boot_if.c
+++ b/common/boot_if.c
@@ -16,9 +16,10 @@
  * the LKD message register should be written by LKD solely.
  *
  * There is only one special case when this function can be used is only when
- * the LKD performs hard reset, which may mean the H/W is not reliable and
- * writing to PCI might not complete and result in the register not cleared.
- * So to be on the safe side, when receiving the WFE, clear the message register
+ * the LKD performs by itself or requests FW to perform hard reset, which may
+ * mean the H/W is not reliable and writing to PCI might not complete and result
+ * in the register not cleared. So to be on the safe side, when receiving the
+ * WFE or RST_DEV command, clear the message register
  */
 void cpu_boot_cmd_clr_before_wfe(void)
 {
